# 💰 Resume Salary Prediction
 
## 📌 Project Overview
 
This project analyzes resume data from HeadHunter and explores factors that influence candidate salary expectations.
 
The objective of the project is to investigate resume characteristics, perform data cleaning and exploratory analysis, and prepare data for future salary prediction models.
 
The project focuses on identifying relationships between candidate profiles and expected salary levels using real-world labor market data.
 
---
 
## 🎯 Project Objectives
 
- Analyze resume data from HeadHunter
- Explore candidate salary expectations
- Clean and preprocess raw data
- Identify patterns and correlations
- Detect outliers and inconsistencies
- Prepare data for machine learning applications
 
---
 
## 📊 Dataset
 
The dataset contains information about job seekers, including:
 
- Expected salary
- Education level
- Employment preferences
- Work experience
- Geographic location
- Professional skills
- Age and demographic information
 
---
 
## 🔍 Project Workflow
 
### 1. Data Structure Analysis
 
- Dataset overview
- Feature inspection
- Data type validation
- Missing value analysis
 
### 2. Data Transformation
 
- Feature engineering
- Missing value handling
- Data normalization
- Format standardization
 
### 3. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
 
- Salary distribution analysis
- Correlation analysis
- Visualization of key relationships
- Candidate profile exploration
 
### 4. Data Cleaning
 
- Outlier detection
- Error correction
- Data consistency validation
 
---
 
## 📈 Key Insights
 
The analysis reveals important relationships between:
 
- Salary expectations and experience
- Salary expectations and education
- Geographic location and compensation
- Candidate qualifications and market value
 
---
 
## 🛠 Technologies
 
- Python
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Seaborn
- Plotly
- Jupyter Notebook
 
---
 
## 🚀 Installation
 
Clone the repository:
 
```bash
git clone https://github.com/Alex1988Den/Resume-Salary-Prediction.git
cd Resume-Salary-Prediction
```
 
Install dependencies:
 
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```
 
Launch Jupyter Notebook:
 
```bash
jupyter notebook
```
 
Open:
 
```text
Resume_Salary_Prediction.ipynb
```
 
and run all cells.
 
---
 
## 💼 Business Value
 
This project demonstrates how resume and labor market data can be analyzed to estimate salary expectations and better understand job market trends.
 
The results may be useful for:
 
- Recruiters
- HR specialists
- Job seekers
- Labor market analysts
- Data Science professionals
 
